versions.changelog:
### Added

- **Puddles you can see.** A post-process pass draws standing water on the road:
  - the tarmac darkened under it;
  - reflections of the cars, barriers and sky;
  - rain ripples.

  It uses the game's own camera every frame, so it works in every camera view. Each pixel is placed in the world from the game's depth buffer, so the puddles stay fixed to the track.
- **Puddles that are the physics.** The same puddle positions drive aquaplaning for every car, so you float exactly where you see water. Puddles form once the track is too wet for intermediates and spread as it floods: up to about 7% of the road under water.
- **Puddles only on the racing surface.** The addon learns the road from where the cars drive and keeps it per track, so from the second session on a track the puddles are there from the first lap.
- **Track panel.** A small on-screen panel says which tyre the track is ready for: Full wets, Intermediates or Slicks. It shows:
  - a wetness bar;
  - your current tyre;
  - a warning when it's too wet for that tyre.

When it says Intermediates, there is no standing water and nothing an inter can't clear anywhere the cars
  are.
- **Tyre-call messages** in the race notification, such as "Track ready for intermediates" and "Too wet for intermediates".
- Settings:
  - **Standing water** (Follows the track / Game);
  - **Puddles you can see** (on / off);
  - **Puddle sync** (ms): only needed if puddles slide at speed on your setup;
  - **Track panel** (Top right / Top left / Bottom right / Bottom left / Off).
